{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm","id":7997,"title":"Dragon-Blooded - My Worries About The Realm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-11T05:51:39-08:00","id":7997,"title":"Dragon-Blooded - My Worries About The Realm","content":"Okay, I have been meaning to write this for sometime now to express my worries about what I think are my biggest gripes about Exalted (and of course it is relative to my favorite ones, the Dragon-Blooded). This problem maybe something that appears exclusively with them because of a very simple reason: they are the only Exalts who exist in a complex, Exalt-filled society that has been running for centuries. When you have something like that, some things are bound to be different, and I don't think the past books have done an exceptional job at getting us inside a society that has demigods working for it left and right.<br /> <br /> <br /> On Charms<br /> <br /> When RPing a Dragon-Blooded within the Realm one of my first doubts is if every Charm is 'catalogued' or if all Charms from the book are just the tip of the iceberg. What do I mean by that? The book has some 200+ Charms? If you are, lets say, a socialite in the Realm, you probably has memorized the ones that could threaten you in the social arena. Does that mean that when a Dragon-Blooded sees a jaded woman passing by they KNOW she has her Jade Defense up? Is it expected? Would using those Charms be expected, considered inpolite? Warlord's Convocation can be used on Dynasts aswell, it is a very powerful Charm. Is it well known? Do young Dragon-Blooded know that when they are called late at night to their general's quarters they are at risk of being turned into slaves?<br /> <br /> These problems arise fast in Dragon-Blooded and they pile up because they are a society, and a very old one at that. There are no more 'secret techniques' if all the Charms t heir kind possesses can be contained in a book. They would be rounded up already. People would know the taps to be sweetened before they even tasted anything in a party, and they would know that when your lover comes to you pissed as hell about something you didn't do that she was the target of Brother Against Brother. Or not? This is not a problem with the ressurging Solars, but it is a problem with the stabilished Dragon-Blooded, in my opinion. When you use Dragon Vortex Attack and shape it like a real Elemental Dragon with the Charm's expansions from the Upright Soldier, do people go &quot;Oh! A Dragon Vortex Attack!&quot; or do they go &quot;AN ELEMENTAL DRAGON! BOW!&quot;. How well known are Charms, how much space for creativity do we have there?<br /> <br /> I would be interested in seeing how this society works. How alchemically improved are the lives of Dragon-Blooded, and from perfumes to narcotics to sexual activities, I need they should be expanded. Solars, Lunars, etc, all need the Charms and skills they have to survive. Dragon-Blooded had centuries to expand on combat-useless stuff, and that is a lot of their flavor, their frivolity and relaxed outlook on a world that is burning around them. I would like to see Charms based around carrying banners in the battlefield, architeture and buildings, cooking, sex, that others do not posses, in the Realm. If we are exploring the Realm, then it makes a lot of sense for us to see how possessing a society can affect demigods, what would they do with their power.<br /> <br /> I know most Charms are designed for real utility, but there should be a few more Charms for cosmetic effects, like manipulating elements and shaping them (something the Dragon-Blooded -still- lack!), from creating buildings and works of art, something in the Water Aspect Charms that could unpoison a water supply, and something in the Air Aspect that could affect the weather or cool the room. I would be interested in learning those things, and the last Realm book was not on par with my expecations.<br /> <br /> <br /> On The Imperial City<br /> <br /> It has been too long since I first started playing Exalted, and I would -really- like to see an unified idea for the Imperial City. How does teh Imperial Manse looks like? Have an artist draw that! How does the city itself looks like? How are the House Manses organized? How do they look? We need a map and interesting locales for the city, far more than it was presented in The Realm. This is the heart of any Dynast chronicle, even if t he players don't live there, that's how important this place is. It deserves a lot of treatement!<br /> <br /> How does the Onyx Curtain works? Do Dragon-Blooded show up to eat at restaurants there like in any normal city in our world? Is it by demand? Do they walk about to relax, or is the habit of walking carelessly with a lover something you only do in the Imperial Manse or outside the Imperial City? Are there theaters? Are the performances boosted by Charms? I have a hard time believing the Dragon-Blooded would book with months notice to see a play where mortals are protagonists, and their cousin with Performance Charms can out do them in a very dramatic way. How does it work? These questions can be expanded and many more can be asked for all the districts. Crimson Delights needs to be fleshed out, and so needs the Temple District. How harsh is the bureaucracy in the Scarlet Empire, is it so crippling that it can effect heroics?<br /> <br /> <br /> On NPCs<br /> <br /> If I could say anything, I would advise you guys to write-in more NPCs like the princess in Thorns and Wisdom Whisperer, people you want to see, flocking around the city. From that wacky, chimera-oriented armor designer (Thundersomething, I forget his name) and his rival, Nazegger, all people who have story hooks you can go with. Many NPCs in Exalted are protagonists, and while that's what I want in a novel, that's not what I want in my game. I need a supporting cast. So aside from social ingame mechanics, I would like to see more rumors about the city and it's denizens, people you read about and go 'I would like to meet this person and solve his problem!' and not 'I would like to meet this person and embark on his quest!', because in the end, the players are the ones who should be followed, not the other way around. I am far more interested, as a player and as a storyteller, in NPCs that I can use as support for my chronicle's most varied aspects, and small concepts can turn into very fun NPCs, like the young son of a General turned historian of war in Cathak that is the family disgrace, and sails off with the PCs in their intrepid new adventure searching for a Cathak artifact, long lost, in hopes his father will accept him! He is just the guy who knows a lot of history, but he has something he cannot achieve without the players (going out of the island would take convincing from the players to the NPC's House, resources to cross the Inner Sea, and a drive to go to adventures) and in the end his conquest is not overshadowing the players. You know you have made someone happy and you have improved the Dynasty a bit by 'healing' that small part of it, with the father accepting his son, and the House recovering an artifact. I would like to see more of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will probably think of more later! But thanks for hearing so far! Of course, as always, this is not an attempt at knocking at the old material, just some ideas on how I would like to see them expanded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:32:51-08:00","id":8016,"title":"","content":"You have some intersting points that should be adressed to some degree. My Dragon-Blooded games have usually avoided the Blessed Isle because of issues like these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:21:51-08:00","id":8045,"title":"","content":"My big hope for the Blessed Isle is that there will be enough going on in cities besides the Imperial City to justify running games there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:32:14-08:00","id":8055,"title":"","content":"Well, I do not know if it's something I imagined or not, but people say that Pangu (where the Palace of Waves is) is one of the places slaves and other people vanish without leaving a trace in the Realm (the reason why Cynis has so many dark secrets is that they provide an enviroment upon which people can live out their darkest fantasies without getting caught). The fact that it's main export is meat (and if I am not mistaken there is also that cult for the Empress there) makes me thing there's a lot of Soylent Green-esque stuff going on in the Imperial Army, where this surplus of meat probably goes to.<br /> <br /> We don't need to run games on the Blessed Isle (although we may), but I think that if you are a Dynast, the Imperial City is going to show up at some point, and right now it is very superficial. It doesn't matter that I am a general in the Scavenger Lands: At some point I will return to the city I was probably raised in, and when I go back, I want to feel in the Realm!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:49:34-08:00","id":8067,"title":"","content":"Re: Usage of Charms/Categorization<br /> <br /> My personal take on it comes from another WW game- I remember back in the day, one of the old V:tM books laid out the common etiquette that it was considered &quot;vulgar&quot; to use social disciplines in an obvious manner on other vampires unless there was a wide gap in station- i.e. the Prince using Dominate on an impertinent Neonate. Passive social boosters weren't just common, they were expected, but it was never couched in the name use of the powers. To translate this into DB society, something like Jade Defense wouldn't be called Jade Defense, it would be referred to in other ways, such as &quot;Don't try and manipulate her, even with the graces of Heshiesh, she will not budge.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T12:22:51-08:00","id":8291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Warlord's Convocation can be used on Dynasts aswell, it is a very powerful Charm. Is it well known? Do young Dragon-Blooded know that when they are called late at night to their general's quarters they are at risk of being turned into slaves? </div> </div> </div>Short answer? No. When a DB has a habit of using this Charm, people don't think: &quot;Oh my gosh, he's using Charm Person to mind control people!&quot; They think: &quot;wow, this person sure is a charismatic leader&quot;. Remember that if you try to use it on someone who has no reason to be loyal to you (or has a reason NOT to be loyal to you), that person is just going to use willpower and resist the Charm.<br /> <br /> I am reasonably hopeful that the changes to the Ex3 social engine will make it less of a gun that makes people your slaves and more something you are encouraged to use when it actually makes sense to use it. I mean, I'm ok with Random Dude McMortal being so taken with the dashing Dragonblood general's charisma that he's willing to help him out, but turning around your worst rival's opinion of you doesn't make sense... unless you actually worked at it to set up an opportunity to use the Charm. Like, something that makes you look worth following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:05:59-08:00","id":8314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8291#post8291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer? No. When a DB has a habit of using this Charm, people don't think: &quot;Oh my gosh, he's using Charm Person to mind control people!&quot; They think: &quot;wow, this person sure is a charismatic leader&quot;. Remember that if you try to use it on someone who has no reason to be loyal to you (or has a reason NOT to be loyal to you), that person is just going to use willpower and resist the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>See? This is one of the things I want to know.<br /> <br /> Lets say my character's father is an accomplished Sesus commander, and he has, like any Elder Dynast worth his commanding salt, Warlord's Convocation. It is one of a kind Charm, and I am inclined to believe that, like his mother/father before him, he would call my character and say &quot;Look, we elder people have a Charm, the Warlord's Convocation. Thing is... that's a mind******* Charm, and it will turn YOU into Cathak Feora's happy little servant. If she calls you for her tent outside other people's view, try to avoid it. Always. You can't learn it now, but one day you'll.&quot;. I mean, the DB society is hundreds and hundreds of years old, I am sure their Charms are -well- known by everyone in the Dynasty (or most of them). So much so that if someone is too dedicated to a general, I would bet that person would get taunted: &quot;Oh, there goes the warlord's convoked!&quot;, wether it's true or not.<br /> <br /> How does the Charm estructure blends in with the society and roleplay in general? I am -very- curious to see that adressed in The Realm, given it's the only book of a society completely dominated by Exalts, the only one of it's kind in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:42:58-08:00","id":8340,"title":"","content":"The idea is that not everyone will think of every Charm -- or necessarily even any Charm, outside Martial Arts -- as a distinct thing or specific technique. This is not always the case -- it might be appropriate for Sidereals to view their Charms as distinct maneuvers, and particularly notable stuff like Deadly Beastman Transformation may be likewise recognized as distinct things -- but seems like a general rule. As above, Warlord's Convocation would probably just be spoken of as someone being incredibly persuasive, drawing on the dragons' blessing to gather devotees to her side.<br /> <br /> Though he speaks of Solar Charms, the idea of power growing out from the character instead of an external thing seems broadly applicable:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am saying Charms, as in Solar Charms, don't exist. They're descriptors for different characters.<br /> <br /> Investigation is Sherlock Holmes, Athletics is Hercules and Jubei and Kenshin. Melee is also Jubei. The entire Night Caste set is Batman.<br /> <br /> When you pick your Charms, you are picking traits you want to attach to your character in order to describe him. Every Charm in there is derived from a character in literature or myth or anime. You aren't using a power to make you Batman, you are using a power because you are Batman.<br /> <br /> The first example is a guy who doesn't really deserve his power, because he didn't earn it, and the second is a guy from whom the power is derived. The essential difference undercuts several arguments posted earlier in the thread, and if you don't understand that, then you probably missed the point.<br /> <br /> They aren't discrete techniques because they do not exist except for us to interface with them. Everyone who experiences such a thing in-game can experience them as a matter of absolutely no outside influence, including training.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:49:16-08:00","id":8345,"title":"","content":"On a related note, I'd like to know more just about what it's like to grow up as a Dynast. They clearly have a fairly solid education, based on the skills of all dynasts, but what about the cultural and social aspects of it?<br /> <br /> Are you likely to be encouraged to spend time with mortals of all stripes, only with Dynast mortals (whether fellow children who may still Exalt, or aging Dynasts who never exalted) regardless of house (and if so, what of the Dynast Terrestrials of other houses?) or only with Dynasts of your own house? How much a role does the Immaculate Faith play in the upbringing of the typical Dynast, and how does this usually shape their stance on the world (especially considering the Immaculate philosophy's stance on why people reincarnate into Terrestrials.) Is there any kind of trouble with pressures surrounding Exaltation? Do teenagers do regularly engage in crazy stuff in an attempt to Exalt, and is that encouraged?<br /> <br /> I imagine answers to such questions would help a lot to get players to shape a better image of their own Dynasts, if nothing else by giving ways to show how their childhood was nonstandard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />All who wish to exist must first accept the existence of things beyond themselves and their current awareness, only then can existence return the favour.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://webchat.sorcery.net/?channels=theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">irc.sorcery.net #theonyxpath</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/236-ina","name":"Ina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar236_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:56:05-08:00","id":8354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8314#post8314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Look, we elder people have a Charm, the Warlord's Convocation. Thing is... that's a mind******* Charm, and it will turn YOU into Cathak Feora's happy little servant. If she calls you for her tent outside other people's view, try to avoid it. Always. You can't learn it now, but one day you'll.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it could be spun a little like:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Cathak Feora's bedroom voice could turn a traitor's ears, to say nothing of its power on those even a little loyal to her. Beware her, but know that (given your pursuits) the Dragons may someday grace </i>your<i> tongue so silver.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:17:52-08:00","id":8394,"title":"","content":"I seems we are getting to one answer, maybe, but I have a very important question if what Metrophelean and Gaius say is true...<br /> <br /> If these are 'stuff we do'... who the hell gives these Charms their complicated names? Not only they feel very 'in setting' they are very theatrical, and I cannot fathom it being just for an OOC-Perspective.<br /> <br /> It's like calling breathing 'The Lifesblood Oxigenation Prana'. It makes no sense unless you want to make it flashy!<br /> <br /> Also, it is not like a society with hundreds of years, with people solely dedicated to exploring Charms, wouldn't catalogue them. People did that with our internal organs, our stars and psychological profiles, why wouldn't they do with 200+ magical abilities that not only are the cornerstone to their grip on power, but limited when compared to the 10,000 dragons that live in the Realm?<br /> <br /> This is all very strange, I'm afraid.... but thanks for the input, guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:40:19-08:00","id":8411,"title":"","content":"I think (and this is speculation) the answer is two-fold (two-fold? who the <i>shit</i> says two-fold?):<br /> <br /> 1) It <i>is</i> theme. The Charms need to be named, so give them thematically appropriate, over-the-top titles to better flavor magic. It's much cooler than MELEE POWER 1, TIER 1. It was mentioned <i>somewhere</i> (though fuck if I can find the source) that the original Charm names were close to as godawful as that example. The choice was made to fix that, because <i>boring.</i><br /> <br /> 2) Legacy. It may have been decided in an earlier edition (in fact, there are references to 'scrolls' and 'books' of Charms in 2e -- but, like Reddit, I'm too lazy to source) that charms were very well categorized. I <i>personally</i> hate this. It's like talking in-character about health levels, or attributes &quot;PRAY LISTEN, MORTAL. FOR MY CHARISMAS ARE RAD LARGE!&quot;<br /> <br /> 2.5) SO YOU CAN SCREAM THEM ALOUD, OF COURSE: <b>HEAVEN-THUNDER DRAGON-GRACED FIVEFOLD-BULWARK GIGATON HAMMER!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":17,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","user":"Metrophelean","date":".  I hate formatting, and wish my brain could just make my text look as pretty as possible. 11-11-2013, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:50:28-08:00","id":8425,"title":"","content":"Oh, and as for the categorization by a long-lived society: I'm sure they have. I'm sure <i>several</i> <i>different, conflicting, politicized, argumentative, nonsensical, fallacious, </i><i>controversial</i> attempts have been made to label all magic, ever. But there's enough leeway in Charm aesthetics (or should be!) and internal Charms that it'd be really hard to hammer down for <i>certain</i>. (For the record, I can totally see <i>Martial Arts</i> being different!)<br /> <br /> I'd think of it a little like a <i>really good track runner</i> and an <i>Olympic</i> <i>track runner</i>. We know one is good, but we've seen almost superhuman feats from the other. Is there a different term for the act of running, or is one just <i>Olympic(Exalted)-level? </i>And we've been running for a <i>long</i> time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:59:40-08:00","id":8433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8394#post8394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these are 'stuff we do'... who the hell gives these Charms their complicated names? Not only they feel very 'in setting' they are very theatrical, and I cannot fathom it being just for an OOC-Perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legend has it that charms originally had really boring, self-evident names until Geoff Grabowski went and rewrote them to make them more interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:33:59-08:00","id":8456,"title":"","content":"I really think this Charm thing should be adressed. Metrophelean raises some good versions, but I would like to see what White Wolf could do it that! Also, Charms are just -part- of what I hope to see in the Realm, so... I guess it's just the tip of the iceberg!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:52:48-08:00","id":8468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8411#post8411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It <i>is</i> theme. The Charms need to be named, so give them thematically appropriate, over-the-top titles to better flavor magic. It's much cooler than MELEE POWER 1, TIER 1. It was mentioned <i>somewhere</i> (though fuck if I can find the source) that the original Charm names were close to as godawful as that example. The choice was made to fix that, because <i>boring.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8433#post8433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legend has it that charms originally had really boring, self-evident names until Geoff Grabowski went and rewrote them to make them more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My extensive research (visiting the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Charms\" target=\"_blank\">Charms section</a> of the What We Know Wiki) bears fruit!<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Charms originally had names like Extra Health Levels (Ox-Body Technique) and Multiple Attacks (Iron Whirlwind Attack), before Geoff went through and renamed them. He didn't change their functions, though. If you had Ox-Body Technique, you were playing a vital person with the constitution of an ox. If you had Iron Whirlwind Attack, you were just playing a guy who was really good at multiple attacks. Charms move in themed strings because they represent skill in certain areas. A character who is a walking blender is represented by putting 24 exp into the Multiple Attacks part of the tree; a guy who is about ki direction puts it into the Solar bolt part of the tree. Each part of the tree is a simplification; a list of purchases that help to depict a character's skill from the lower end to the upper end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also,<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Legacy. It may have been decided in an earlier edition (in fact, there are references to 'scrolls' and 'books' of Charms in 2e -- but, like Reddit, I'm too lazy to source) that charms were very well categorized. I <i>personally</i> hate this. It's like talking in-character about health levels, or attributes &quot;PRAY LISTEN, MORTAL. FOR MY CHARISMAS ARE RAD LARGE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool coyote-avatared dude's personal sensibilities align with mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:48:08-08:00","id":8498,"title":"","content":"Although they have only been briefly mentioned by John, I think the &quot;bloodline charms&quot; will help a lot to depict the fact that DB society has been around for a long time and that their lineages have advanced in different ways.<br /> <br /> Biologicaly speaking, DB's are the only kind of exaltation prone to evolve. I don't mean this in a pokemon sense in which evolution equals more power. I mean that throughout DB history, custom uses of essence (I mean creation of new charms) could have been discovered by different individuals who have passed them down only to their descendants. <br /> <br /> I really hope to see that some families are able to use cool charm trees and be distinguished for that. Just like Toph is famous for being the first earth bender to bend metal, so can DB families be recognized for such feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T22:39:22-08:00","id":8624,"title":"","content":"To expand on what I said earlier: your character doesn't wake up one day and think &quot;I really want to learn Warlord's Convocation! I can use it to influence people!&quot; Rather, you, as the player, think &quot;My character is a charismatic leader of men who can easily win the loyalties of people. To represent this mechanically, I will use the Warlord's Convocation Charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> I will also join Metrophelean and Gaius and say that, most of the time, I really dislike the idea of characters using Charms by name. A Dawn doesn't know he's using the Charm Fire and Stones Strike any more than a D&amp;D fighter knows he's using the feat Power Attack. Though there are exceptions. For example, I figure that the ability to see Essence is probably called the All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight in some First Age texts. Actually, it probably has a bunch of other fancy names, too, because people in Creation like fancy names. Most of the time, though, people wouldn't actually use that name (even if they know about it): they're just going to say they can see Essence.<br /> <br /> This is also depends a lot on the type of being. Sidereals have more Charms that are flavorful to name in-charcter: I fully encourage a Sidereal to explain that he used the Earth and Sky Bargain to speed his recovery after a grave injury. A Jadeborn Warrior Caste who has fully mastered the Fivefold Embodiment of Jade should be able to brag about it. And an Alchemical would be downright disappointing if he couldn't point on his body and say &quot;this is my Electrification Onslaught Dynamo, that one is my Momentum Redirection Pulse Injector...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:26:24-08:00","id":8716,"title":"","content":"I subscribe to the John Morke idea of Charms. You won't find them insetting in the Exalted world, since they're just abilities and characteristics of the character, an extension of their power. They aren't referred to as Charms by characters within setting at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:48:01-08:00","id":8724,"title":"","content":"As many have mentioned, Charms are NOT spells like in Dungeons &amp; Dragons.<br /> Charms are like they are for the players benefits and because we need some mechanics to describe the characters, that's all.<br /> In-Universe, they are application of Essence to various abilities the character ALREADY possess. That is why most charms have an Essence and a Skill requirement. You must ALREADY be a silver tongued charmer to learn how to use Essence to make your natural charm even better.<br /> <br /> That is why the only things that could be recognized, in the core book of 2E, were Combos. Obvious charms were just an obvious use of Essence, ie. you could see the guy was using magic, but not what type, but Combos had names and special poses/gestures/moves that a rival could identify and then understand what the combo did.<br /> <br /> However, Essence is definitely something that exist in-universe and is well understood, especially in the Realm. So while young dragon blooded might not be told directly &quot;beware of the charm X&quot;, they would be aware to a point that people can do X, Y and Z through use of Essence.<br /> <br /> The Devs have already stated about the new Dragon Blooded that we will see differences of note in the various Dynastic houses, maybe up to have exclusive charm lines common only to certain houses. Those would be the equivalent of secret training techniques that teach a dragon blooded to shape his Essence in certain specific ways and when united with mundane training, can obtain unique results.<br /> <br /> This statement also bode well for having more details about the internal working of The Realm as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/616-volkmar","name":"volkmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar616_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T05:20:34-08:00","id":8735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>volkmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8724#post8724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As many have mentioned, Charms are NOT spells like in Dungeons &amp; Dragons.<br /> Charms are like they are for the players benefits and because we need some mechanics to describe the characters, that's all.<br /> In-Universe, they are application of Essence to various abilities the character ALREADY possess. That is why most charms have an Essence and a Skill requirement. You must ALREADY be a silver tongued charmer to learn how to use Essence to make your natural charm even better.</div> </div> </div> </div> And yet, the deliberative meeting hall of the Old Realm had symbols float above your head to identify your charm usage. That's the only case where I've seen the actual books take a side on this old argument. Dev opinions, especially dev opinions from people that weren't present at the time of those books' writing are just that - opinions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I rather find it stupid that observation wouldn't have led the DBs to codify their magical charms over the past few centuries. It makes far more sense to me - especially when teaching people charms is a thing that happens. How on earth could you teach your students Jade Defense, having learned it from your teacher, and knowing that every other school also teaches a very similar technique without coming up with a name for it? Humans don't work like that - heck, we even came up with a name for flicking your wrist to deflect a blow whilst fencing; and the opening moves in chess are practically all categorized and named.<br /> <br /> In short, I don't buy that &quot;she's just really good at ignoring my arguments&quot; would be said, without immediately being followed by someone else going &quot;yeah, probably has Jade Defense up&quot;. Substitute your own names if you want flavor, so your family might call it the Serenity of the Mountain Technique, or whatever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> There is no such thing as innocence, only degrees of guilt.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/71-sidmen","name":"Sidmen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar71_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T05:45:18-08:00","id":8742,"title":"","content":"Well, a thesis that charms are personal feats of ability and Essence manipulation is as strong as easy it is to customise and create new charms. Because let's be honset here- if you can't create new charms or change existing ones in a meaningful way, then every character will have the same charms and that creates an impretion that they are indeed distinctive techniques that you can categorise and teach.<br /> <br /> The alternative is making charms less numerous, but also broader and customizable visually so they can feel like they are different for each person. But this seems to be the opposite of what the Devs are doing with charms.<br /> <br /> And then you have Dynastic Charms, Sorcerous Charms, Supernatural Martial Arts and a huge part of Sidreal Charms, which ARE distinctive techniques you can categorise and teach. We're left in this nebulous space where most of the charms are NOT distinctive and singular techniques, but the charmsets as a whole are not really well equiped to model every single possible power an individual can have and there are also charms that ARE distinctive and singular, but follow exactly the same rules as those that AREN'T. It's terribly confusing.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea that every charm is a power singular to the individual who developed it. But while making them so crunchy, you just can't make enough of them to account for every single ability a character might want to have, so there should be solid and easy guidelines to creating custom charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","user":"Arrakiz","date":". 11-12-2013, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/620-arrakiz","name":"Arrakiz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar620_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T06:35:54-08:00","id":8765,"title":"","content":"While I expect <i>What Fire Has Wrought</i> to be like this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8425#post8425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and as for the categorization by a long-lived society: I'm sure they have. I'm sure <i>several</i> <i>different, conflicting, politicized, argumentative, nonsensical, fallacious, </i><i>controversial</i> attempts have been made to label all magic, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this makes much more sense:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidmen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8735#post8735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally, I rather find it stupid that observation wouldn't have led the DBs to codify their magical charms over the past few centuries. It makes far more sense to me - especially when teaching people charms is a thing that happens. How on earth could you teach your students Jade Defense, having learned it from your teacher, and knowing that every other school also teaches a very similar technique without coming up with a name for it? Humans don't work like that - heck, we even came up with a name for flicking your wrist to deflect a blow whilst fencing; and the opening moves in chess are practically all categorized and named.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the 'innate' conception of charms, but that doesn't entail that they can't be systematically characterized, named, whatever. Terms like &quot;riposte&quot; describe a fairly large category of physical movements, but it's a certainly an intelligible idea; it makes sense to give the whole family of things a name (in the same way that it might makes sense to name a charm). Similarly, we can (and the Greeks did) put all sorts of names to various sorts of moves that can be made in conversation or argumentation (RHETORIC in da house!), and that makes a lot of sense as well.<br /> <br /> Having charm codices, primers and whatnot on the twists of Essence known to produce certain sorts of effects in the world, is, in my estimation, just too useful, too doable, and in man's nature to ignore. As I said, while I expect that such things will be &quot;conflicting, politicized, argumentative, nonsensical, and fallacious,&quot; the Realm doesn't have to be comically inept about <i>everything</i>. There are too many examples of ancient societies, from Egypt to Greece to China, being extraordinarily thoughtful and precise in their conception and categorization of phenomena in the world (even which those societies did not understand the underlying facts of science of those phenomena) to make the 'innate' conception of charms outside the realm of codification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidmen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8735#post8735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In short, I don't buy that &quot;she's just really good at ignoring my arguments&quot; would be said, without immediately being followed by someone else going &quot;yeah, probably has Jade Defense up&quot;. Substitute your own names if you want flavor, so your family might call it the Serenity of the Mountain Technique, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAlso, something like this. It's like when you pose a trivia question to a group of friends, and someone comes back two minutes later with an answer... you suspect that your friend may have employed Google and Cellphone Trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","user":"Equitable Remedy","date":". 11-12-2013, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:22:48-08:00","id":8789,"title":"","content":"Sidmen and Equitable Remedy mirror my feelings exactly.<br /> <br /> It is one thing to say Solars don't do it, but Solars don't have an Exalt Society for thousands of years. Dragon-Blooded did have time to expand on that.<br /> <br /> I want their society to be fleshed out, damn it! And I think this could be a nice way of doing so. Not that it needs to be this way, but I think it should be adressed!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Equitable Remedy's take on how he expects What Fire Has Wrought to be, I say this: me too, but it's lazy. It's too lazy to slap a 'They are incompetent' excuse, even if the Scarlet Empire has been the world's most powerful modern organization and was led by a woman White Wolf has always told was -very- capable.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are not as stupid as some books would have you believe, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","user":"Tchokes","date":". 11-12-2013, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:35:10-08:00","id":8837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8789#post8789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Equitable Remedy's take on how he expects What Fire Has Wrought to be, I say this: me too, but it's lazy. It's too lazy to slap a 'They are incompetent' excuse, even if the Scarlet Empire has been the world's most powerful modern organization and was led by a woman White Wolf has always told was -very- capable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scarlet Empress <i>is</i> incredibly capable... at getting things how she likes them. Note that this will not necessarily be the same as peak effectiveness as we would call it. In many places, it is certain not to be. She structured the Realm -- introducing deliberate inefficiencies into its inner workings -- so that it would collapse without her.<br /> <br /> I can see her taking completely trivial things like what exactly to call Charms* and turning them into yet more tools to pit multiple Houses against each other. Possibly multiple times during her reign. I imagine it would amuse her.<br /> <br /> * Assuming again, despite the huge variety of ways many of them can manifest, that you take each and every Charm as a completely distinct thing and settle on one and precisely one dominant name in-setting for each. I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 11-12-2013, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:15:25-08:00","id":8866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8765#post8765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having charm codices, primers and whatnot on the twists of Essence known to produce certain sorts of effects in the world, is, in my estimation, just too useful, too doable, and in man's nature to ignore. As I said, while I expect that such things will be &quot;conflicting, politicized, argumentative, nonsensical, and fallacious,&quot; the Realm doesn't have to be comically inept about <i>everything</i>. There are too many examples of ancient societies, from Egypt to Greece to China, being extraordinarily thoughtful and precise in their conception and categorization of phenomena in the world (even which those societies did not understand the underlying facts of science of those phenomena) to make the 'innate' conception of charms outside the realm of codification.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Realm is comically inept, at all. Given a society that raises its most physically, mentally and spiritually powerful citizens as the highest form of enlightenment, keeps their actions towards the much larger population of mortals mostly consequence-free, and exists in a constant state of civil cold war, it's still the highest functioning authority in Creation. The Realm is my single favorite part of the world's infrastructure.<br /> <br /> That said, every sorcerous, studious Dragon-Blooded philosopher with any interest in the codification of Charms is likely to be met with an equally sorcerous, studious Dragon-Blooded philosopher of another House. Charm codex after Charm codex would be met by refuting claims and special-interests-driven intrigue. Settling on a name would be all but impossible, given the power and importance of Charms like <i>Wind-Carried Words</i> and the imagery of <i>Dragon-Graced Weapon</i>. Who gets to decide? Are there religious connotations that might worry the <i>Mouth of Peace? </i>There's a lot going on, and given how our own real-world philosophers, religious mystics and men of science butt heads over dogma and evidence, it's not even a stretch to imagine a culture built on in-fighting and politics would do the same.<br /> <br /> But let me be totally clear: I <i>like</i> the idea that a magical society might try to codify the similar &quot;powers&quot; of its mightiest. I just don't dig that these codifications are presented as-is from the book in which we, the players, get them.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure I buy the idea that the Charms as we're presented with them <i>are</i> exactly the same. Who's to say that Cynis Rokan and Mnemon Aedis, both Earth-Aspect Dragon-Blooded with grand goremauls and <i>Dragon-Graced Weapon</i> are, in-setting, using a similar power? I'll admit that <i>second-edition</i> leans that way, but that edition <i>does</i> codify its Charms. Charms <i>are</i> a thing that Exalted can study.<br /> <br /> But I'm getting dangerously close to a gamist/narrativist/simulationist argument, and no one wants or needs that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":17,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","user":"Metrophelean","date":". 11-12-2013, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:03:19-08:00","id":8907,"title":"","content":"Related to the point that there are no 'secret' techniques, I think that there will always be confusion about one is capable of and just what someone is trained in. Mentors color the training of their pupils, after all. I think the use of magic in a fashion that does not support the society may often be viewed as gauche. There was a reference in the 2E book about 'Brother against Brother Insinuation' (or some charm like that) being considered a faux pas or even crime in society.<br /> <br /> In any case, though I think I rambled, I just want to say that DB are going to expect some use of magic, some use of magic is going to be considered 'over the top, and DBs are always going to scumbag sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/87-faller3","name":"Faller3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:09:11-08:00","id":8915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8837#post8837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Empress <i>is</i> incredibly capable... at getting things how she likes them. Note that this will not necessarily be the same as peak effectiveness as we would call it. In many places, it is certain not to be. She structured the Realm -- introducing deliberate inefficiencies into its inner workings -- so that it would collapse without her.<br /> <br /> I can see her taking completely trivial things like what exactly to call Charms* and turning them into yet more tools to pit multiple Houses against each other. Possibly multiple times during her reign. I imagine it would amuse her.<br /> <br /> * Assuming again, despite the huge variety of ways many of them can manifest, that you take each and every Charm as a completely distinct thing and settle on one and precisely one dominant name in-setting for each. I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree to an extent, but although the Dynasty has inefficient aspects (The Thousand Mazy Paths anyone?) it's rulers, the Dragon-Blooded, are raised for excellency. They are trained rigorously in a very draconian, Darwinist society, and while they might not get things done easily, any lesser creature would have made the Empire implode by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:38:37-08:00","id":8941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>volkmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8724#post8724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As many have mentioned, Charms are NOT spells like in Dungeons &amp; Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although sadly they're presented like them, and obliged to be memorized and referred to and nitpicked like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T10:41:21-08:00","id":8945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8915#post8915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree to an extent, but although the Dynasty has inefficient aspects (The Thousand Mazy Paths anyone?) it's rulers, the Dragon-Blooded, are raised for excellency. They are trained rigorously in a very draconian, Darwinist society, and while they might not get things done easily, any lesser creature would have made the Empire implode by now.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, we're mostly agreeing on this. Many in the Realm are incredibly competent and efficient; the Realm would have been dust without them. My point was that efficiency isn't an end unto itself. Some of the bureaucratic inefficiency stems from intentionally putting incompetent people there, while some stems from the enormously skilled people <i>trying</i> to do their best and running up against the structure the Empress set up around them. She has intentionally created a system that is not a hallmark of efficiency from what we imagine an ideal government would be.* This is because she created the system to be very efficient at keeping her indispensable, and it does that very well. She has exerted tremendous skill and done an impeccable job of meeting the goal she wanted to achieve.<br /> <br /> * <i>Please</i> let us not turn this into a political debate about <i>what </i>that should be.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt many Dynasts constantly ask themselves, &quot;What is the best way to go about this task?&quot; and try to do that. They just also need to balance that out to some degree with, among others, &quot;What does the Empress want out of this?&quot; and &quot;What does my House want out of this?&quot; where answers to these questions may not line up nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T11:29:00-08:00","id":9006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8945#post8945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, we're mostly agreeing on this. Many in the Realm are incredibly competent and efficient; the Realm would have been dust without them. My point was that efficiency isn't an end unto itself. Some of the bureaucratic inefficiency stems from intentionally putting incompetent people there, while some stems from the enormously skilled people <i>trying</i> to do their best and running up against the structure the Empress set up around them. She has intentionally created a system that is not a hallmark of efficiency from what we imagine an ideal government would be.* This is because she created the system to be very efficient at keeping her indispensable, and it does that very well. She has exerted tremendous skill and done an impeccable job of meeting the goal she wanted to achieve.<br /> <br /> * <i>Please</i> let us not turn this into a political debate about <i>what </i>that should be.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt many Dynasts constantly ask themselves, &quot;What is the best way to go about this task?&quot; and try to do that. They just also need to balance that out to some degree with, among others, &quot;What does the Empress want out of this?&quot; and &quot;What does my House want out of this?&quot; where answers to these questions may not line up nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lol, no doubt! I agree with you and I am not trying to make a debate out of it! XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T11:36:31-08:00","id":9014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=9006#post9006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lol, no doubt! I agree with you and I am not trying to make a debate out of it! XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, sorry about the redundant info-dump, then. ^_^ Had a hunch we were on the same page. One just sometimes gets a little trigger-happy with the walls o' text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:42:35-08:00","id":9388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidmen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=8735#post8735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet, the deliberative meeting hall of the Old Realm had symbols float above your head to identify your charm usage. That's the only case where I've seen the actual books take a side on this old argument. Dev opinions, especially dev opinions from people that weren't present at the time of those books' writing are just that - opinions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I rather find it stupid that observation wouldn't have led the DBs to codify their magical charms over the past few centuries. It makes far more sense to me - especially when teaching people charms is a thing that happens. How on earth could you teach your students Jade Defense, having learned it from your teacher, and knowing that every other school also teaches a very similar technique without coming up with a name for it? Humans don't work like that - heck, we even came up with a name for flicking your wrist to deflect a blow whilst fencing; and the opening moves in chess are practically all categorized and named.<br /> <br /> In short, I don't buy that &quot;she's just really good at ignoring my arguments&quot; would be said, without immediately being followed by someone else going &quot;yeah, probably has Jade Defense up&quot;. Substitute your own names if you want flavor, so your family might call it the Serenity of the Mountain Technique, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in a structured culture that passes down knowledge of skills it is likely they will have a name they use for that skill so they can talk about it, for example: 'Hey, did you hear about how the son of Random Dynastic Rival was so incompetent that he managed to burn down their dojo trying to master elemental burst? What shame he has brought upon his house!' On the other hand an Exalt that more or less has to work things out on their own (like most solars and exigents) is only going to have an in setting name for their charms if they feel like it, the names in the core book will be purely for the benefit of the people playing the game so they know that the Dawn just popped out an essence fueled flurry attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T00:14:01-08:00","id":62031,"title":"","content":"First off, let me say this to anyone reading this. I am not griping at any of the 3e Developers <i>(3eD)</i> -- please don't take anything that I'm writing in that vein. The below are just some simple desires, based off of things that I have seen in the previous editions of Exalted. I know that developing games <i>(or writing anything for that matter)</i> is not as easy as waving a wand and making it happen. I also know that you guys <i>(and gals)</i> work hard, and it is fully appreciated. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm#post7997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have been meaning to write this for sometime now to express my worries about what I think are my biggest gripes about Exalted (and of course it is relative to my favorite ones, the Dragon-Blooded). This problem maybe something that appears exclusively with them because of a very simple reason: they are the only Exalts who exist in a complex, Exalt-filled society that has been running for centuries. When you have something like that, some things are bound to be different, and I don't think the past books have done an exceptional job at getting us inside a society that has demigods working for it left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let us not forget about Lookshy. There are a few others <i>(Maybe they will get expanded or new one's added?)</i>, but they tend to be smaller and ultimately they are not &quot;Big Players&quot; on the world stage <i>(Ok...the Forest Witches might be, but they are just weird and would be considered Anathema as far as the rest of Creation is concerned...)</i><br /> <br /> Lookshy is a very well organized and populous nation. It's society is complex, and it's Dragon-Blooded numerous in comparison to their population: 1 DB per 100 mortals <i>(At least according to the previous editions. Things may change in 3e, which is ok.)</i> Not to mention the number of 1st Age Artifacts they have. <i>(Again, this may change in 3e...)</i><br /> <br /> As for your concerns...&quot;Sigh&quot;...I'm with you on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm#post7997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Charms<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">When RPing a Dragon-Blooded within the Realm one of my first doubts is if every Charm is 'catalogued' or if all Charms from the book are just the tip of the iceberg. What do I mean by that? The book has some 200+ Charms? If you are, lets say, a socialite in the Realm, you probably has memorized the ones that could threaten you in the social arena. Does that mean that when a Dragon-Blooded sees a jaded woman passing by they KNOW she has her Jade Defense up? Is it expected? Would using those Charms be expected, considered inpolite? Warlord's Convocation can be used on Dynasts aswell, it is a very powerful Charm. Is it well known? Do young Dragon-Blooded know that when they are called late at night to their general's quarters they are at risk of being turned into slaves?<br /> <br /> These problems arise fast in Dragon-Blooded and they pile up because they are a society, and a very old one at that. There are no more 'secret techniques' if all the Charms t heir kind possesses can be contained in a book. They would be rounded up already. People would know the taps to be sweetened before they even tasted anything in a party, and they would know that when your lover comes to you pissed as hell about something you didn't do that she was the target of Brother Against Brother. Or not? This is not a problem with the ressurging Solars, but it is a problem with the stabilished Dragon-Blooded, in my opinion. When you use Dragon Vortex Attack and shape it like a real Elemental Dragon with the Charm's expansions from the Upright Soldier, do people go &quot;Oh! A Dragon Vortex Attack!&quot; or do they go &quot;AN ELEMENTAL DRAGON! BOW!&quot;. How well known are Charms, how much space for creativity do we have there?<br /> <br /> I would be interested in seeing how this society works. How alchemically improved are the lives of Dragon-Blooded, and from perfumes to narcotics to sexual activities, I need they should be expanded. Solars, Lunars, etc, all need the Charms and skills they have to survive. Dragon-Blooded had centuries to expand on combat-useless stuff, and that is a lot of their flavor, their frivolity and relaxed outlook on a world that is burning around them. I would like to see Charms based around carrying banners in the battlefield, architeture and buildings, cooking, sex, that others do not posses, in the Realm. If we are exploring the Realm, then it makes a lot of sense for us to see how possessing a society can affect demigods, what would they do with their power.<br /> <br /> I know most Charms are designed for real utility, but there should be a few more Charms for cosmetic effects, like manipulating elements and shaping them (something the Dragon-Blooded -still- lack!), from creating buildings and works of art, something in the Water Aspect Charms that could unpoison a water supply, and something in the Air Aspect that could affect the weather or cool the room. I would be interested in learning those things, and the last Realm book was not on par with my expecations.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that, among the Dragon-Blooded, Charms would be &quot;known&quot; -- perhaps individual Charm might be called by different names, but at least the more &quot;common&quot; ones would be the subject of study and, perhaps in some of the more risque parts of society, discussed or actually displayed in very &quot;unique&quot; ways <i>(ie: Cynus parties with certain &quot;Performance Charms&quot;).</i><br /> <br /> Like you I would like an expansion of the Charm Sets <i>(You called them &quot;Cosmetic effects,&quot; but a &quot;Battlefield Banner&quot; charm would be very useful if it rallied troops and relayed information without the enemy knowing. And don't discount any architecture Charms -- especially when it comes to building Manses).</i> I want my Dragon-Bloods, both PCs and NPCs, to be able to do great things with their Charms, no matter their chosen field/skills.<br /> <br /> And while we are on the subject of Charms: Grievous Wound Alteration Energy converts Aggravated to Lethal; Wound-Closing Touch converts Lethal to Bashing; there isn't one that does anything for bashing. I get that Dragon-Blooded aren't &quot;Healers&quot;...but come on, they should be able to heal bashing in themselves or others. &quot;Sigh&quot;...I house-ruled this in my game <i>(along with many other new Charms...)</i>, but it seemed an oddity to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm#post7997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On The Imperial City<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It has been too long since I first started playing Exalted, and I would -really- like to see an unified idea for the Imperial City. How does teh Imperial Manse looks like? Have an artist draw that! How does the city itself looks like? How are the House Manses organized? How do they look? We need a map and interesting locales for the city, far more than it was presented in The Realm. This is the heart of any Dynast chronicle, even if t he players don't live there, that's how important this place is. It deserves a lot of treatement!<br /> <br /> How does the Onyx Curtain works? Do Dragon-Blooded show up to eat at restaurants there like in any normal city in our world? Is it by demand? Do they walk about to relax, or is the habit of walking carelessly with a lover something you only do in the Imperial Manse or outside the Imperial City? Are there theaters? Are the performances boosted by Charms? I have a hard time believing the Dragon-Blooded would book with months notice to see a play where mortals are protagonists, and their cousin with Performance Charms can out do them in a very dramatic way. How does it work? These questions can be expanded and many more can be asked for all the districts. Crimson Delights needs to be fleshed out, and so needs the Temple District. How harsh is the bureaucracy in the Scarlet Empire, is it so crippling that it can effect heroics?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon-Blooded or Blessed Isle book(s) <i>(Whatever eventually comes out)</i> can have a short section on the Imperial City -- the book(s) can't cover everything.<br /> <br /> However, I would like to see the Imperial City have it's own book, complete with a detailed map, in-depth history, in-depth description of each section of the city, NPCs, etc. Yes, I am asking (and dreaming) for a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tchokes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm#post7997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On NPCs<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If I could say anything, I would advise you guys to write-in more NPCs like the princess in Thorns and Wisdom Whisperer, people you want to see, flocking around the city. From that wacky, chimera-oriented armor designer (Thundersomething, I forget his name) and his rival, Nazegger, all people who have story hooks you can go with. Many NPCs in Exalted are protagonists, and while that's what I want in a novel, that's not what I want in my game. I need a supporting cast. So aside from social ingame mechanics, I would like to see more rumors about the city and it's denizens, people you read about and go 'I would like to meet this person and solve his problem!' and not 'I would like to meet this person and embark on his quest!', because in the end, the players are the ones who should be followed, not the other way around. I am far more interested, as a player and as a storyteller, in NPCs that I can use as support for my chronicle's most varied aspects, and small concepts can turn into very fun NPCs, like the young son of a General turned historian of war in Cathak that is the family disgrace, and sails off with the PCs in their intrepid new adventure searching for a Cathak artifact, long lost, in hopes his father will accept him! He is just the guy who knows a lot of history, but he has something he cannot achieve without the players (going out of the island would take convincing from the players to the NPC's House, resources to cross the Inner Sea, and a drive to go to adventures) and in the end his conquest is not overshadowing the players. You know you have made someone happy and you have improved the Dynasty a bit by 'healing' that small part of it, with the father accepting his son, and the House recovering an artifact. I would like to see more of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will probably think of more later! But thanks for hearing so far! Of course, as always, this is not an attempt at knocking at the old material, just some ideas on how I would like to see them expanded.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the NPCs. If they can't be full writeups then provide more info than a name. My desire would be to at the very least provide a quick blurb on NPCs: Name <i>(DoB, DoE, DoD, Location, Interests)</i> -- Shorthand: DoB = Date of Birth; DoE = Date of Exaltation; DoD = Date of Death; Location &amp; Interests are self-explanatory. If desired a &quot;Template&quot; could be provided, similar to the one for Gods, with a &quot;Ranking&quot; system, so that Storytellers could quickly provide stats for the NPCs if they need too. This would keep the page-count down, while providing more world info. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> More on NPCs (And things in general, actually...): When mentioning things in the NPCs background/description it would help to know why they dislike someone. For example: In The Outcastes <i>(I know...1e here, but there are similar things in 2e...),</i> under the Forest Witches, Cevis Ghandarva's feelings &quot;toward the Ledaal family, in particular, remain bitter.&quot; In the Outcaste this is the only mention of the Ledaal, with no other explanation of why. In MAP-DB, under the Forest Witches, it talks about how the Sidereal caught on to what Cevis Ghandarva was doing -- so I figured that the Ledaal flushed him out. But it took two different books, from two different editions to do this. &quot;Sigh&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More Thoughts:<br /> <br /> Consistency:<br /> One of the things that frustrates me is that there are inconsistencies between books. Not between editions -- that's going to happen. Between different books of the same edition. One book will mention something as happening on a particular date, and another will have it happening on another date. Another book will have slightly different events than another book. Now, none of these are &quot;In Character&quot; -- they are up-front, and &quot;Out of Character&quot; writings. I just ask for consistency, as much as humanly possible, between all the books <i>(I know that this is difficult, and that I am asking a lot...)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> A Timeline:<br /> Please...A unified Timeline. It helps when people want to run a game set at some other point in the History of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Blessed Isle<br /> I would like to see the Prefectures expanded upon, and the actual number written about expanded. It would be nice if the level of detail was expanded, with which House controls/influences each detailed <i>(be explicit -- not coy here).</i> An in-depth map of the Blessed Isle would be nice. Individual cities, with maps provided <i>(one-page would be fine).</i> A calendar, replete with Holidays - both secular and religious - would also be nice <i>(though, that would be asking a lot...).</i> The Thousand Scales: Expand &amp; List the different portions of the Bureaucracy -- with their overlapping functions <i>(A convoluted &quot;map&quot; of functions would be fun)</i>. The Legions: A list of which legions exist, where they are stationed, who the General's are, with a quick Blurp on them <i>(and perhaps a write-up on the most important ones)</i>. The Immaculate Order: Show other places beyond the Palace Sublime. Primary Schools: List several, with a Blurb about each. <i> (I could go on...)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The Houses:<br /> They should get write-ups in whatever &quot;Main Book&quot; comes out <i>(Dragon-Blood, Blessed-Isle, etc...)</i>, however I'd like to see a &quot;House&quot; book. Not sure if there should be a separate one for each House or one overarching &quot;Houses of the Realm.&quot; Either way, subjects covered should be History, Movers/Shakers, Interests, Prominent NPCs, &quot;Black Sheep,&quot; Family Trees, Unique &quot;Powers&quot; <i>(Charms, Sorcery, Artifacts),</i> Alliances, Enemies, House Secrets. Among other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Satrapies:<br /> Expanded upon, more added. Tell us who they are, what their culture is like, who lives there, what their interactions with the Realm and the surrounding region is like. What do they do? Provide NPCs, History, a compelling story for us.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hundred Kingdoms:<br /> Yes, Virginia. I want a Hundred Kingdoms book. I want little ones, medium ones, big ones. I want pastorial, peaceful kingdoms. I want tyrannical overlords, and benevolent rulers. I want intrigue. I want...Adventure!<br /> <br /> <br /> Exalted:<br /> This is the most important thing for me. I want that excitement back. I want that Warm Fuzzy Glow that I had when I first picked up Exalted &quot;Way Back When.&quot; Can I get that with 3e? Please?<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T00:54:07-08:00","id":62042,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the more inhuman a charm is, the more likely it is that it's cataloged.<br /> <br /> For example, I see no reason why Jade Defense would be talked about as a specific charm or supernatural ability. There's lots of times when people have approached me and attempted to sell me something or convince me of something and I've found myself bored. If a Dragon Blood can see that mortals sometimes get bored when people try to sell them things, why would they assume that their own boredom is a specific essence manipulation?<br /> <br /> Sure, a tutor might teach a young Dragon-Blood how to put on an air of polite indifference when someone is trying to manipulate them, but that tutor could easily be a non-Exalted.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, tossing lightning from your hands is something humans can't do. In fact, it comes far more naturally to air aspect DBs than fire or water aspect ones. Elemental Bolt Attack will probably be thought of as a 'charm' though its name could change from place to place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T02:27:13-08:00","id":62050,"title":"","content":"Random thought: A book giving multiple example names for Charms would add some wordcount (bad) but would drive home a message about &quot;not all people call a given effect the same name&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T03:02:54-08:00","id":62060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62050#post62050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought: A book giving multiple example names for Charms would add some wordcount (bad) but would drive home a message about &quot;not all people call a given effect the same name&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sidebar explaining the same would be just as good, minus the wordcount issues and the potential confusion of actually naming the mechanical bits inconsistently throughout the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T04:07:42-08:00","id":62075,"title":"","content":"I remember that the first edition Dragon Blooded book stated the charms were so cheap because they had been refined and retaught over many generations over and over. It seemed pretty clear that there was a limited number of &quot;known&quot; charms and I suppose they would be catalogued well. If I am misremembering, I apologize.<br /> <br /> Personally I slightly prefer their charms to be something you could go read up on in a library. They would be called by the names in the book or ones similar to them, just as there would be dozens or even hundreds of entirely non-magical techniques taught to smiths or scribes with names ending in &quot;Technique&quot; or something like that.<br /> Instead of calling it folding steel, it might be called &quot;Folding Steel Technique&quot; or &quot;Binding the Metal Pages Treatment&quot; or something like that. Such names were created for entirely non-magical procedures, to help the students memorize and remember every step. Just like such names make it (weirdly) easier for us to remember specific charm names.<br /> <br /> So, to conclude: I think they'd be called by those names, and be research-able but would somewhat sink into the background of the conversation. Many Dynasts may have to go to the library to figure out which of &quot;Dropping Snow Technique&quot; and &quot;Shaping Hand Style&quot; was referring to a way to prepare eggs and which was a Craft charm.<br /> <br /> Basically people proficient in something would recognize the names of the things they've either been studying or preparing to study. To everyone else, it's just professionals being pretentious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:40:17-08:00","id":62098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edward Eldritch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62075#post62075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that the first edition Dragon Blooded book stated the charms were so cheap because they had been refined and retaught over many generations over and over. It seemed pretty clear that there was a limited number of &quot;known&quot; charms and I suppose they would be catalogued well. If I am misremembering, I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the First Edition corebook, and while it was a neat idea, it was also pretty incoherent, since your Solars are out there generally with no support and no mentors-- certainly no older Solar mentors, nor manuals, nor anything else. If Charms are commonly a thing that are codified and refined, shouldn't the Solars be starting from scratch?<br /> <br /> Ditto the outcaste who Exalts on a farm somewhere out in the Haslanti League-- if that's how it works, shouldn't his instinctively-grasped Charms be crude and inefficient compared to the polished magic practiced in the Imperial City? And yet clearly this is not something the books are going to do-- it would require a massive duplication of wordcount for the sake of making 'independent' characters massively crappier. That's not fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:57:30-08:00","id":62109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62098#post62098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the First Edition corebook, and while it was a neat idea, it was also pretty incoherent, since your Solars are out there generally with no support and no mentors-- certainly no older Solar mentors, nor manuals, nor anything else. If Charms are commonly a thing that are codified and refined, shouldn't the Solars be starting from scratch?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the corebook addressed that, more or less, by saying that the refinement was 'remembered' by your Essence from your past incarnations, which also opened the door for knowing things like Martial Arts styles because you knew them in a past life.<br /> <br /> It didn't really address the issue about Dragon-Blooded Outcastes, but if you went that route you could probably reasonably argue that the blood remembers, since Terrestrials are already doing a Lamarkian inheritance thing a lot of the time. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:33:21-08:00","id":62131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62109#post62109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, the corebook addressed that, more or less, by saying that the refinement was 'remembered' by your Essence from your past incarnations, which also opened the door for knowing things like Martial Arts styles because you knew them in a past life.<br /> <br /> It didn't really address the issue about Dragon-Blooded Outcastes, but if you went that route you could probably reasonably argue that the blood remembers, since Terrestrials are already doing a Lamarkian inheritance thing a lot of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or simply that Creation remembers - that over time the repetition of certain magical patterns has cut indelible channels into the Essence of the etc. etc. As ever, &quot;find fluff to justify it&quot; isn't much of a sticking point.<br /> <br /> Still, I can see justifications for cutting that particular bit of flavor - makes running an Early First Age game messier, for one.<br /> <br /> (I would add my voice to those saying that something can be both an innate talent and part of a systematic scheme of techniques, and that it doesn't make a darn lick of sense for the Realm especially not to have at least one of the latter for describing Charms. Thus, you can both do what feels natural, working out for yourself how to manipulate your Essence, <i>and</i> be practicing the Monkey Blows A Raspberry Prana.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:38:37-08:00","id":62132,"title":"","content":"Really, as a way to preempt the idea that players can't come up with custom Charms that are just published Charms with lower mote costs and/or higher numbers, it seems a bit less efficient than just not bringing the issue up and letting the STs handle it with their own sensibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:47:14-08:00","id":62302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62042#post62042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that the more inhuman a charm is, the more likely it is that it's cataloged.<br /> <br /> For example, I see no reason why Jade Defense would be talked about as a specific charm or supernatural ability. There's lots of times when people have approached me and attempted to sell me something or convince me of something and I've found myself bored. If a Dragon Blood can see that mortals sometimes get bored when people try to sell them things, why would they assume that their own boredom is a specific essence manipulation?<br /> <br /> Sure, a tutor might teach a young Dragon-Blood how to put on an air of polite indifference when someone is trying to manipulate them, but that tutor could easily be a non-Exalted.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, tossing lightning from your hands is something humans can't do. In fact, it comes far more naturally to air aspect DBs than fire or water aspect ones. Elemental Bolt Attack will probably be thought of as a 'charm' though its name could change from place to place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obvious vs Inobvsious. Plus, if a DB or group of DBs is/are &quot;known&quot; for a particular Charm or set of Charms <i>(even and Inobvious one)</i> among other DBs. There might be &quot;suspicions&quot;...unless Essence can be seen -- which was inborn in 1e but not 2e, and we'll have to see about 3e.<br /> <br /> I do think that there is a Bureau that has attempted to codify the various &quot;Charms&quot; of the DBs, though. Complete with various subdivisions providing yearly reports, and competing with each other. This could be where that &quot;flowery names&quot; come from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:15:57-08:00","id":62331,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, as I have in previous threads like this, that the 'intuitive knowledge' aspect of 3e... and the removal of things like Charm manuals... is a huge mistake and is not authentic to the feel and atmosphere of previous editions.<br /> <br /> I feel that the stimulationist argument of 'Oh, but this makes the world not make sense' is pretty weak as well. We never had any issues with logic embolisms while we were having great fun in the heavily wuxia-influenced world it portrays.<br /> <br /> As I said to John in the first thread where he announced this rather impressive change, Ninja Scrolls was literally like THE movie that enabled me to put my first group together - 'Just like Ninja Scrolls!'. And the way they were trading techniques, discussing each others unique techniques, all of that was massively evocative and interesting.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of that, rather than somehow embracing it and making it 'cool' in 3e, was a huge mistake that I will immediately fix with homebrew and retconning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:53:24-08:00","id":62349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62098#post62098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the First Edition corebook, and while it was a neat idea, it was also pretty incoherent, since your Solars are out there generally with no support and no mentors-- certainly no older Solar mentors, nor manuals, nor anything else. If Charms are commonly a thing that are codified and refined, shouldn't the Solars be starting from scratch?<br /> <br /> Ditto the outcaste who Exalts on a farm somewhere out in the Haslanti League-- if that's how it works, shouldn't his instinctively-grasped Charms be crude and inefficient compared to the polished magic practiced in the Imperial City? And yet clearly this is not something the books are going to do-- it would require a massive duplication of wordcount for the sake of making 'independent' characters massively crappier. That's not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to hear you come out and say it. Clears alot of things for me. Put also sad face (I get the reasin though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:01:30-08:00","id":62354,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Exaltation, and then on the individual Exalted.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals obviously have highly codified and extremely Charm manuals. Sidereals might as well, given the nature of their Charms and the Martial Arts motif.<br /> <br /> Solars? I don't see why they would, and it certainly wouldn't matter if they did, since the knowledge would be long lost in the forgotten ruins of the First Age. Even then, it can go either way. I can play a Solar Himura Kenshin who has very specific charm techniques and combinations, but I can also play Solar Hercules, whose magic powers never get more specific than &quot;really strong dude.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are going to be even more varied. Between bloodline-specific charms and the teachings of ancient Immaculate Masters, there's plenty of room for rare Charms that express an extremely advanced mastery of Essence, but some of the most basic charms aren't going to be worth codifying, both because they're so prevalent that they're normalized within Dragon-Blooded society and because they're not much more impressive than what mortals can do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:45:52-08:00","id":62392,"title":"","content":"I think low-level Charms will be an even mix: Ox-Body will probably not be specificelly codified other than &quot;use Essence to strengthen your body young one&quot; while Elemental Bolt and Wind Carrying Words (or whatever it's called) would be more codified: they are extremely useful and versatile, so getting them down to textbook level is probably needed. Of course the big question is whether Dragongraced Weapon/Arrow is taught as one Charm or a different one... for Fire aspects it maybe about honing your passion, while for Earth aspects it's about wielding your stoicness with your weapon or whatever...<br /> <br /> Higher level Charms are taught more on a master-apprentice level imho, so there's even more variance there, especially since for example Jaded X (forgot its name) can be taught as &quot;learn how to focus your negative energies into an impenetrable shield against or manipulation&quot; or &quot;remember the most boring moment of your life... now wrap some Essence around that&quot;, so I don't think that's exactly codified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:47:35-08:00","id":62393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62354#post62354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Exaltation, and then on the individual Exalted.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals obviously have highly codified and extremely Charm manuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>And interchangeable too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62354#post62354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals might as well, given the nature of their Charms and the Martial Arts motif.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the Sidereal Charms were &quot;set in stone&quot; and new one's couldn't be developed <i>(at least in 1e &amp; 2e -- won't even speculate for 3e...).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62354#post62354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars? I don't see why they would, and it certainly wouldn't matter if they did, since the knowledge would be long lost in the forgotten ruins of the First Age. Even then, it can go either way. I can play a Solar Himura Kenshin who has very specific charm techniques and combinations, but I can also play Solar Hercules, whose magic powers never get more specific than &quot;really strong dude.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also think that Solars could call upon past lives to recall long lost knowledge and Charms <i>(ie: to justify spending experience).</i> This also be a method to allow the Solar to find these forgotten ruins, and thus recover the information...but that sounds more like a Twilight thing to recover Spells than a method to recover &quot;long-lost Charms...&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that individual Solars probably developed off-shoots that they kept hidden from their fellow Solars, and this information would have to be recovered in ancient ruins. But the &quot;common Charms&quot; (if there is such a thing) could be remembered from past lives <i>(say the Charms in the main book...otherwise, being a lone Solar would suck even more than it already does...).</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62354#post62354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded are going to be even more varied. Between bloodline-specific charms and the teachings of ancient Immaculate Masters, there's plenty of room for rare Charms that express an extremely advanced mastery of Essence, but some of the most basic charms aren't going to be worth codifying, both because they're so prevalent that they're normalized within Dragon-Blooded society and because they're not much more impressive than what mortals can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part I like - House Charm Set! It just makes sense. Sort of like Japanese Samuarai styles or the fighting styles of Europe <i>(Not that the Charm Sets need to be all about fighting...they shouldn't...).</i> Each House having their own Charm Set will help each House feel more unique and provide more RP opportunities, especially if more background is provided on the House.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T14:32:58-08:00","id":62468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62098#post62098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the First Edition corebook, and while it was a neat idea, it was also pretty incoherent, since your Solars are out there generally with no support and no mentors-- certainly no older Solar mentors, nor manuals, nor anything else. If Charms are commonly a thing that are codified and refined, shouldn't the Solars be starting from scratch?<br /> <br /> Ditto the outcaste who Exalts on a farm somewhere out in the Haslanti League-- if that's how it works, shouldn't his instinctively-grasped Charms be crude and inefficient compared to the polished magic practiced in the Imperial City? And yet clearly this is not something the books are going to do-- it would require a massive duplication of wordcount for the sake of making 'independent' characters massively crappier. That's not fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>1m surcharge or the equivalent to Charms you learned yourself (that is, with no mentor) until you've used it X times/had if for Y time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:22:34-08:00","id":62503,"title":"","content":"As good a solution as any, right? But... honestly, why worry about it too much? As we always say, story over narrative. We don't really need to justify the fact that charms have changed over the centuries in the fiction but haven't any mechanical adjustments currently ; if that DOES bother us, we can always homebrew that.<br /> <br /> Solar charm 'techniques' and manuals enable cool characters. They let characters talk about interesting things and add distinctive, fun shit to the titles they claim ('I developed MAJESTIC THUNDER BLAM!'). I've literally had dozens of PCs do this. I've had PCs describe sections of downtime where they retreated from foes as getting into contact with ancient memories and learning lost techniques of Solar-Fu. I've gotten huge mileage out of Solars finding old charm manuals from past incarnations.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Invisible Fortress had a few of these!<br /> <br /> This change in 3e bugs me for these reasons. It seems like the 'story first' philosophy isn't being used here which is frustrating. I get the simulationist arguments against it, why it 'doesn't make sense', I just don't care and when I didn't care previously it didn't impede my fun or suspension of disbelief in any real measurable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:40:06-08:00","id":62520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62503#post62503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As good a solution as any, right? But... honestly, why worry about it too much? As we always say, story over narrative. We don't really need to justify the fact that charms have changed over the centuries in the fiction but haven't any mechanical adjustments currently ; if that DOES bother us, we can always homebrew that.<br /> <br /> Solar charm 'techniques' and manuals enable cool characters. They let characters talk about interesting things and add distinctive, fun shit to the titles they claim ('I developed MAJESTIC THUNDER BLAM!'). I've literally had dozens of PCs do this. I've had PCs describe sections of downtime where they retreated from foes as getting into contact with ancient memories and learning lost techniques of Solar-Fu. I've gotten huge mileage out of Solars finding old charm manuals from past incarnations.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Invisible Fortress had a few of these!<br /> <br /> This change in 3e bugs me for these reasons. It seems like the 'story first' philosophy isn't being used here which is frustrating. I get the simulationist arguments against it, why it 'doesn't make sense', I just don't care and when I didn't care previously it didn't impede my fun or suspension of disbelief in any real measurable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you, sort of, considered that maybe it's not that big of a deal? It might sound strange but, can't we have both?<br /> <br /> Sure, I'd greatly appreciate if the books clarified which charms are descriptive techniques and which are just broad generalizations about powers multiple different individuals develop on their own in different ways... But honestly, you can do that on your own can't you? It doesn't strike me as terribly difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T16:03:37-08:00","id":62531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62503#post62503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This change in 3e bugs me for these reasons. It seems like the 'story first' philosophy isn't being used here which is frustrating. I get the simulationist arguments against it, why it 'doesn't make sense', I just don't care and when I didn't care previously it didn't impede my fun or suspension of disbelief in any real measurable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take heart, for it's like 90% probable that the &quot;no Charm manuals&quot; thing will take the shape of <i>not mentioning Charm manuals</i> rather than blanket prohibitions of the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T16:23:15-08:00","id":62542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62503#post62503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This change in 3e bugs me for these reasons. It seems like the 'story first' philosophy isn't being used here which is frustrating. I get the simulationist arguments against it, why it 'doesn't make sense', I just don't care and when I didn't care previously it didn't impede my fun or suspension of disbelief in any real measurable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My perspective on it is that if it isn't handled very, very carefully, &quot;Solar charms are discrete objects* which can be codified in manuals&quot; can imply that charms are a function of the Solar <i>Exaltation</i> rather than a function of the Solar <i>Exalted</i>, which shifts the focus of the game from the characters to their powers, which in turn encourages discussions of &quot;Solar shards,&quot; &quot;supermotes,&quot; &quot;divine power batteries,&quot; &quot;cosmic lottery&quot; and a heap of other irrelevant fanon, which ultimately results in the Solar Exalted being displaced and overshadowed by their own Exaltation. From a design standpoint, &quot;Yurgen Kaneko shot a Sidereal in the head with an arrow from a thousand miles away&quot; is much more interesting and relevant &quot;Yurgen Kaneko killed a Sidereal from a thousand miles away with Accuracy Without Distance and the 1st Archery Excellency.&quot; <br /> <br /> The idea works for Alchemicals because it's part of their design philosophy and they run with, but I'm not sure if it would work nearly as well for the other Exalted. <br /> <br /> The players can have manuals of Solar charms, but I don't think the developers should be the ones to introduce the idea. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Not necessarily a physical object, but an &quot;object of study.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T16:56:21-08:00","id":62572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62531#post62531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take heart, for it's like 90% probable that the &quot;no Charm manuals&quot; thing will take the shape of <i>not mentioning Charm manuals</i> rather than blanket prohibitions of the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my takeaway, too. Toward the end of the lengthy conversation in which this whole thing first arose with John (starts relatively early in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Charms#Solar_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> with Hippokrene's comment), he explicitly said this wasn't something that especially bothered him. And from a little later:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether you see it your way or mine won't change how the Charms work mechanically.<br /> <br /> But a Solar who just Exalted in Nexus can complete the entire Dawn Charmset without ever meeting another Solar, without knowing what the Solars were/are, and without any exposure to First Age lore or past lives.<br /> <br /> The Charm set is not external, waiting for him to discover it. So he has no idea what the names of any of these Charms are. He exists in a complete vacuum, and the game supports this\u2014if he is a Dawn, he needs no training. If he can learn the Charms without training, and can learn the Charms without knowing their names, and is not automatically Exalted with a full codex of Charm names (which he is not) then you might conclude that the &quot;Charms&quot; (he may not even think of them as Charms) he has learned have completely different names and methods and pathos from the exact (mechanically) same Charms of another Solar, regardless that these two Solars were modeled by the same Charm set, the same mechanics, the same names.<br /> <br /> IE, the names of Charms, and even Charms themselves don't qualify as anything important or crucial or necessary. They are just character descriptors.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with the concept of a character who gains a particular Charm and the player fluffs it as a technique learned from a manual or legendary scroll (with/without the same name as the Charm). There's nothing wrong with the concept of a character who gains the same Charm and the player fluffs it as a different technique said character has devised (with/without the same name as the Charm). There's nothing wrong with the concept of a character who gains the exact same Charm and the player fluffs it not as an explicit technique at all, simply a mark of the character's refined skill/capabilities/whatever. It's entirely possible for all of a given character's various Charms to each be fluffed in entirely different ways.<br /> <br /> Saying all Charms are very definitely discrete things in-setting is more limiting to possible stories than just letting the Charms be names and mechanics that can indeed be that, or can be whatever interpretation a given player/table wants them to be. Saying in the book that they are explicitly <i>not</i> discrete things in-setting would likewise step on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Clarity, rewording, etc. 01-31-2014, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:09:26-08:00","id":62583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62531#post62531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take heart, for it's like 90% probable that the &quot;no Charm manuals&quot; thing will take the shape of <i>not mentioning Charm manuals</i> rather than blanket prohibitions of the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah pretty much. If all goes well, you won't even notice that we never bring up the possible existence/nonexistence of Charm manuals because you'll be too interested in the stuff we <i>do</i> talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:19:03-08:00","id":62594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62583#post62583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah pretty much. If all goes well, you won't even notice that we never bring up the possible existence/nonexistence of Charm manuals because you'll be too interested in the stuff we <i>do</i> talk about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give us, like, a couple of months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:46:06-08:00","id":62608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/7997-dragon-blooded-my-worries-about-the-realm?p=62583#post62583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah pretty much. If all goes well, you won't even notice that we never bring up the possible existence/nonexistence of Charm manuals because you'll be too interested in the stuff we <i>do</i> talk about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one am looking forward to 3e. I can't wait <i>(Well I can wait, and will, especially if waiting halps to make 3e a better product.)</i><br /> <br /> Thanks kind Mr Sheppard.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}